{"condition": "B1", "run_id": "B1-dev-revised-rubric", "checkpoint": "nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-BF16", "question_id": "financebench_id_00438", "document_id": "ADOBE_2022_10K", "split": "dev", "training_seed": null, "sampling_seed": null, "derived": false, "evaluation_signature": "98485d04e7dc272169fa2d62058475ceb00a57bb28167a728f778ef2f0aa61cf", "F": 1.0, "A": 0.0, "G": 1.0, "Ret": 1.0, "correct": 0, "grounded_success": 0, "reward": 0.0, "unresolved": true, "grader_version": "workshop-rubric-v2-derived-provenance", "fabricated_citation": false, "judge_error": "RuntimeError", "stop_reason": "accepted_finish", "output_tokens": 1805, "total_reward": 0.0, "turns": 6, "submission": {"answer_type": "text", "value": "", "unit": "", "scale": "", "decision": "", "answer_text": "As of Adobe's FY2022 (year ended December\u202f2,\u202f2022), the company reported operating income of $6,098\u202fmillion against total revenue of $17,606\u202fmillion, yielding an operating margin of approximately **34.6\u202f%**.  \n\nFor comparison, Adobe's prior fiscal year (FY2021) reported operating income of $5,802\u202fmillion on revenue of $15,785\u202fmillion, giving an operating margin of about **36.8\u202f%**. In FY2020 the operating margin was roughly **32.9\u202f%** (operating income $4,237\u202fmillion on revenue $12,868\u202fmillion).\n\n**Trend:**  \n- FY2020 \u2192 FY2021: operating margin improved (32.9\u202f% \u2192 36.8\u202f%).  \n- FY2021 \u2192 FY2022: operating margin declined (36.8\u202f% \u2192 34.6\u202f%).  \n\nThus, as of FY2022 Adobe does **not** show a clearly improving operating\u2011margin profile on a year\u2011over\u2011year basis; the most recent year saw a modest dip after a prior year increase.\n\n**Why operating margin may be a less\u2011telling metric for Adobe:**  \n- Adobe\u2019s business is high\u2011margin, subscription\u2011driven software; a large portion of costs are fixed (R&D, sales & marketing) and spread over growing revenue, so operating margin can be influenced more by strategic investments and product\u2011mix shifts than by operational efficiency alone.  \n- Significant non\u2011operating items (e.g., acquisition\u2011related amortization, restructuring, and tax effects) can distort the picture.  \n- Investors often focus on gross margin, free\u2011cash\u2011flow margin, and non\u2011GAAP metrics (such as adjusted EBITDA) for a clearer view of the underlying software\u2011as\u2011a\u2011service profitability.\n\n**Sources:** Adobe Inc. 2022 Form\u202f10\u2011K, Consolidated Statements of Income, page\u202f54 (receipt\u202fr3).", "citations": [{"receipt_id": "r3", "document_id": "ADOBE_2022_10K", "page": 54}], "calc_id": ""}, "latency_s": 10.890534436000053, "tool_calls": 6, "calculator_used": false, "gold_page_read": true, "citation_count": 1, "visible_citations": 1, "raw_tool_chars": [2455, 1342, 2481, 1649, 96, 1838], "visible_tool_chars": [2506, 1393, 2532, 1700, 145, 1889], "truncated_observations": 0, "cost_usd": null, "trace_path": "results/paper_2026_rl4llm/B1-dev-revised-rubric/rollouts/financebench_id_00438.json"}
